<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Creoda of Mercia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Creoda is named in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> royal genealogies as an early king of Mercia, a great-grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/icel">Icel</a>, the father of Pybba and the grandfather of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia">Penda</a>. Later chronicles place his reign in the late 6th century, around 585 to 593, but no contemporary record survives, and he is regarded as a semi-legendary figure.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/creoda-of-mercia.jpg" alt="Creoda of Mercia" width="320" height="254" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Speed · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Creda_-_John_Speed.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
